cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use MARS, please cite the specific archived software version you used
  as well as the associated paper. See README.md for availability and
  citation details.
title: "MARS: A Lightweight Morphology-Aware RFI Segmentation Network for Mask-Guided Mitigation in Radio Astronomy"
type: software
version: 0.1.1
date-released: 2026-09-23
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Haalandspring/MARS"
url: "https://github.com/Haalandspring/MARS"
abstract: >-
  MARS (Morphology-Aware RFI Segmentation) provides a lightweight neural
  network and a GPU-based pipeline for radio-frequency interference
  segmentation and mask-guided mitigation of 8-bit SIGPROC filterbank
  observations. The repository includes the inference source, configuration,
  trained checkpoint, dependency specifications, and TensorRT compilation
  and verification code.
keywords:
  - radio astronomy
  - radio-frequency interference
  - segmentation
  - pulsars
  - fast radio bursts
  - GPU computing
